type represents a frame or fretboard diagram used together with a chord symbol. The representation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is based on the NIFF guitar grid with additional information. The frame type’s unplayed attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"what to display above a string that has no associated frame-note element. Typical values are x and the empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string. If the attribute is not present, the display of the unplayed string is application-defined.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlframe","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame","kind":"symbol","title":"MXLFrame","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFrame","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFrame","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"title":"MXLTenths","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the middle of a staff line."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFrame/width":{"title":"width","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"width"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text